00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:58,509
You can write a couple jokes
about the homeless.

233
00:11:58,592 --> 00:11:59,468
How much?

234
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:01,762
It's a charity event.

235
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:05,850
I already give money to the Palestinians.
I'm stretched too thin as it is.

236
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,893
[Denise] You make jokes about the homeless
all the time.

237
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:10,354
-Just give me one.
-I don't feel comfortable about this.

238
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,481
-It's not like they'll be there.
-Hey.

239
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:16,068
-Denise, could I talk to you?
-Sure, how's my girl doing?

240
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:18,779
-Hanging tough, right?
-She's doing well.

241
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:22,867
I think she's nervous about
this kissing scene with Jayke, you know?

242
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:25,703
I was thinking maybe there's something
we can do to help her.

243
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:27,872
Maybe get some mom advice?

244
00:12:27,955 --> 00:12:32,418
Uh... No. No. I mean, she's 14,
and she is batshit crazy,

245
00:12:32,501 --> 00:12:35,379
and she doesn't talk to me anymore,
so, I can't.

246
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:37,923
No. You gotta step away,
let her ride it out.

247
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:41,135
Okay. I just wanted to make sure
Arya felt good about the scene.

248
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:42,511
You know what? She's gonna be fine.

249
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:43,596
[cell phone buzzes]

250
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:45,514
-I have to take this, okay?
-Okay.

251
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:48,726
Hey, Jen.
Are you going to SoulCycle tonight?

252
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:50,978
Concerned about your daughter.
That's all.

253
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:54,315
Is the bread gluten-free?

254
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:58,777
No. It's bread. Normal bread.
Bread-bread. There's gluten in the bread.

255
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,321
Do you have Ezekiel bread?

256
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:02,531
-"Ezekiel bread"?
-Yeah.

257
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:06,076
There's two types of bread, white bread
and brown bread. Pick a side.

258
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,579
You know what, are these berries organic?

259
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:11,874
Dude, organic is a lie.
That's corporate interest, man.

260
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:14,168
It's fine. The carrots will work.

261
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:15,920
Bugs Bunny, eat the Twizzlers.

262
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:18,589
-I don't like Twizzlers.
-Eat. Hey!

263
00:13:18,672 --> 00:13:21,091
Hey, what's up, Mr. C?

264
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:24,094
Mr. C? I like that, that's very cool.

265
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:26,597
I just wanted to ask you
for a little favor.

266
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:30,601
Arya's stressing out about the scene
you're shooting later today.

267
00:13:30,684 --> 00:13:31,894
-Yeah?
-Yeah, yeah.

268
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:35,856
I was thinking maybe the two of you
could get together, rehearse.

269
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,191
It might help her out.

270
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:39,068
Plus, you haven't
spent much time together.

271
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:40,611
Yeah, yeah. I know.

272
00:13:40,694 --> 00:13:43,948
I've been busy with the show and my music.

273
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:46,492
I also spend ten hours a week
on my self-care.

274
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:48,953
Wow. Ten hours. That's a lot.

275
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:49,954
[both chuckle]

276
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:53,582
-Uh... So, could you?
-Yeah. I'll rehearse with her.

277
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:54,833
-For sure.
-All right.

278
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:58,087
Hey, look at that 1,000-kilowatt smile
on that guy.

279
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:00,589
Thanks.

280
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:01,966
[Gus chuckles]

281
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:05,094
As your friend, I got to let you know
you sound like a pedophile sometimes.

282
00:14:05,177 --> 00:14:08,347
I know. I realized
as it was coming out of my mouth.

283
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:12,226
His smile? Way too specific.
It's like you've been studying his mouth.

284
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:13,644
Get out his face. He's a preteen.

285
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:14,979
-His nuts haven't dropped yet.
-Right.

286
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:17,147
I got your note, Kev. Thank you.

287
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:26,323
I don't know how to tell you this,
so I'm gonna come out with it.

288
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,575
There aren't a lot of people.

289
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,743
What do you mean?
Give me a ballpark.

290
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:33,872
If there was a ballpark that held
four people, it would be sold out.

291
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:37,918
Fucking shit! Four people?
There's four fucking people in there?

292
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:41,463
You always said if you could reach
just one person then...

293
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:44,758
I didn't literally just mean
one person, okay?

294
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:46,051
I'm not going in.

295
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,721
I hope you have a plan to fix this,
considering it is your fault.

296
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:50,389
-My fault?
-Yes.

297
00:14:50,472 --> 00:14:52,516
If you weren't spending
so much time with Stella,

298
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,684
you could've promoted this.

299
00:14:53,767 --> 00:14:56,020
Why don't we call it off?
We can go home.

300
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:59,064
You're telling me,
in a city of millions of people,

301
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:01,358
you can't find 40 that need help?

302
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:03,652
How will I find 40 people
in the next half hour

303
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:04,570
to come into this thing?

304
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:08,908
I don't know, but you better do it.
Fill it up! Fill it up, Mickey!

305
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:10,618
All right. I will!

306
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:12,620
All right. Fill it up!

307
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:19,460
Hi! Could I interest you in coming in here
and listening to--

308
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:20,628
I have an appointment.

309
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,550
Hey, I don't really need to hear all
of the rejections.

310
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:29,303
-Okay.
-Maybe take it down there, huh?

311
00:15:29,386 --> 00:15:30,930
All right. I'm gonna figure this out.

312
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:41,482
[Arya] "Now we've got nine dead
on our side, because I wasn't there."

313
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:44,026
"Fine. You want the real answer?"

314
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:45,903
"We don't have time for anything else."

315
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:49,573
"I'd rather lose nine of them
than one of you. Okay?"

316
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:51,075
"What did you say?"

317
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:53,619
"I can live without them,
but I can't live without you."

318
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:58,332
-And then we kiss. Cool! All right.
-Yep.

319
00:15:58,415 --> 00:16:00,876
[chuckles] Sorry, I'm not the best actor

320
00:16:00,959 --> 00:16:02,503
-Shut up. You're amazing.
-for you to do this with.

321
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:04,964
[stammers] You've got it.

322
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:08,092
You're amazing, and then...
I don't know. [chuckles]

323
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:10,010
You're the best in the new cast.

324
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:13,931
Thanks. You don't have to say that.
It's not a competition.

325
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:16,892
-A little bit.
-Yeah. [chuckles]

326
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:21,772
-I heard you do music.
-Really? How'd you know that?

327
00:16:21,855 --> 00:16:24,483
I mean, there's a giant organ
right behind you! [laughs]

328
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:28,946
[laughs] Okay. Yeah, I bring it with me,
